  "description": "The Prolights EVO 160F is a static fresnel fixture with a square housing, probably about 0.21 by 0.28 by 0.18 metres. A pan hinge at the root carries a yoke arm, roughly 20.5 by 25 by 4 units, which holds a tilt hinge at its top. The square head mounts under that hinge as one unit with a single lens and light. Pan and tilt are both manual-aim axes with a nominal 360-degree range, and tilt swings the head, lens and emitter together. The front optic is one circular Fresnel lens disc filling the head face, with a single LED source centred behind it. There is one controllable intensity cell. A rear control panel is probably fitted but is not modelled.",
